# Used by docker compose and deploy/init-tls.sh. Copy to .env and edit.

# Optional for plain HTTP: nginx answers on any host name when unset.
# DOMAIN=game.example.com

# --- HTTPS (optional) -------------------------------------------------------
# Set DOMAIN above plus the two lines below, then run ./deploy/init-tls.sh once.
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.tls.yml
# EMAIL=you@example.com
# Test against Let's Encrypt staging first (no rate limits, untrusted cert):
# STAGING=1

# --- Monitoring panel (optional) --------------------------------------------
# Serves the Colyseus room/client inspector at http://<host>/monitor behind HTTP
# basic auth. Without MONITOR_PASSWORD the panel is not mounted at all in
# production, so a misconfigured deploy can never expose it unprotected.
# MONITOR_USER=admin
# MONITOR_PASSWORD=change-me

# --- Profiling panel (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# Serves the CPU/heap profiling admin page at http://<host>/admin behind HTTP
# basic auth. Same gating as the monitor: without ADMIN_PASSWORD it is not
# mounted at all in production. Snapshots are written to ADMIN_SNAPSHOT_DIR
# (defaults to a directory under the system temp dir).
# ADMIN_USER=admin
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me
# ADMIN_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/tmp/tank-arena-snapshots

# --- Client build (not read by docker compose) ------------------------------
# Inlined into the client by apps/client/build.ts. Only needed when the client
# is hosted on a different origin than the game server.
# PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=wss://game.example.com
